# WEBSITE_ASSETS — Public Web Property Exception
#
# Logline: Bounded carve-out for browser-facing assets and installers that cannot be .oo/.oot.
#
# Setup: Referenced by openOODA/scripts/enforcer.oo. Authorizes formats that browsers and GitHub Pages require.
#
# Beats:
#   1. Declare directories and authorized artifact formats.
#   2. State invariants that keep product source out of these directories.
#   3. Define the canonical install scripts.
#   4. Make this exception permanent and self-contained.

## 1. Scope

The following directories are the public web property of the openOODA project:

- `openOODA.github.io/` — GitHub Pages root, static site, guides, playground, WASM demos
- `install/` — install portal (if present)
- `registry/` — package registry pages (if present)
- `research/` — research portal pages (if present)
- `brand/` — brand assets (if present)

## 2. Authorized Artifact Formats

Browser and host tooling require these formats in the web property:

- `.html` — static pages
- `.js` — client-side scripts (CSP-reviewed)
- `.css` — stylesheets
- `.wasm` — compiled `.oo` binaries produced by `oodac`
- `.svg` — vector graphics
- `.png` — raster images
- `.ps1` — Windows install script
- `.txt` — `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt`, `robots.txt`, human-readable metadata
- `.nojekyll`, `CNAME` — GitHub Pages control files

## 3. Invariants

- No product source code, compiler modules, standard-library code, or runtime code may be placed in these directories.
- The only shell scripts permitted are the canonical public installers: `openOODA.github.io/install.sh` and `openOODA.github.io/install.ps1`.
- All `.wasm` files must be produced from `.oo` sources by `oodac`.
- All `.html` files must be static or generated from `.oot` docs by the SSG.
- No `.py`, `.rb`, `.pl`, `.md`, `.c`, or `.h` files may be added to the web property.

## 4. Exit Criteria

This exception is permanent. Browsers, GitHub Pages, Windows PowerShell, and web crawlers require these formats.
